"playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1526, "last_played": 1693544313, "avatar": "e27f10e7e54aaf1a3d4d6a2be934cd5796275a83"}, "language": "english", "review": "Really was enjoying the game, until they completely broke Origin. Now even though its in my library, EA is convinced I dont own it. Even tried getting the EA subscription to play it through that, except oh wait, EA can detect its in my library, so I need to install it to play. Except WAIT, EA thinks I dont own it. Asks me for a product key, I bought it through Steam so I check there, except Steam says I bought it elsewhere, so they dont have a key. All of this to force me to buy the remastered version, EA as a company sucks, and you can bet I wont be shilling out more money to them just for the remastered version. Let me play the game I own, or give me my money back. If I buy it through Steam, it should run through Steam, I shouldn't need a separate app to launch it, otherwise buying through steam is literally useless", "timestamp_created": 1693870729, "timestamp_updated": 1693870729, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 20, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.613128602504730225", "comment_count": 1, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887286", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "145625848", "author": {"steamid": "76561198011514532", "personaname": "OdoG", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198011514532/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 62, "playtime_forever": 7, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 7, "last_played": 1672037651, "avatar": "96bb9858974070c59a66b46587dc5c9738a309e8"}, "language": "english", "review": "Broken.  Doesn't work.", "timestamp_created": 1693786059, "timestamp_updated": 1693786059, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 18, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.607081830